s and which stephen  replies i think i can and he gets a  little bit of confidence and he starts  hyping himself starts talking to the  jackal he says float like a butterfly  sting like a bee which is what muhammad  ali said the world heavyweight boxing  champion and steven has the confidence  and the jackal even jumps at him and  steven stands his ground and manages to  punch the jackal in the face with a huge  blow now unfortunately steven gets a  little cocky here and the jackal  continues to rough him up however an  incoming car is coming and steven  manages to throw the jackal into the car  right before it hits them and you can  see that the car is super messed up from  hitting the jackal further confirming  the jackal is real but people just can't  see it now from here mark talks to  steven again of course through a  reflection and he actually gives him a  little bit of praise he tells him that  was a hell of a punch but mark tells  stephen that he needs to look around  people could get hurt if he doesn't give  him the body and good old stephen  doesn't want to risk anyone getting hurt  so he gives control to mark and now we  see the true moon knight come out in the  ceremonial armor and we see him take his  crescents off of his chest which in the  comics are actually made out of  adamantium which in the comics is also  what wolverine's claws are made out of  and if you notice here moon knight can't  fly or jump really high and he pretty  much can't do anything that's super we  see him climb up the wall not jump up it  or fly but climb like a normal human he  kind of just gets super strength and the  suit provides them with increased  durability and it heals him but besides  that he doesn't have a lot of massive  powers but we see him lead the jackal  away jumping from the rooftops we see  the classic moon knight jump in front of  the crescent moon and his powers once  upon a time in the comics did depend on  the moon cycle but they ended up  changing that so 